From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: WebGPU only with ENABLE(WEBGPU)

The Amiga port has no WebGPU (ENABLE_WEBGPU off, no WebGPU
implementation), but WebCore still built its WebGPU bindings and module:
their IDLs carried no Conditional, so 148 JSGPU* bindings, the GPU*
classes and the inspector's WebGPU paths were all in the engine (about
1.5 MB of 68k code). With this patch they build only with ENABLE(WEBGPU):

- Every Modules/WebGPU IDL and GPUCanvasContext.idl is Conditional=WEBGPU,
  so the generated bindings are empty without it, and Navigator's `gpu`
  attribute goes with the NavigatorGPU mixin.
- GPUCanvasContext leaves the RenderingContext and OffscreenRenderingContext
  unions (IDL and C++), and getContext("webgpu") returns null.
- The Modules/WebGPU sources and JSGPUErrorCustom.cpp build only with
  ENABLE(WEBGPU); GPUDevice is an EventTarget only then.
- Navigator keeps no GPU without a WebGPU implementation, as WorkerNavigator
  already did.
- The console's canvas recording and the inspector's canvas agent, canvas
  call tracer, recording arguments and shader programs keep their WebGPU
  paths only with ENABLE(WEBGPU); without it a shader program reports no
  source and cannot be edited or highlighted.

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/Modules/WebGPU/GPU.cpp b/Source/WebCore/Modules/WebGPU/GPU.cpp
index a33d541d13d..c72aea91b6b 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/Modules/WebGPU/GPU.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/Modules/WebGPU/GPU.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@
  */
 
 #include "config.h"
+
+#if ENABLE(WEBGPU)
 #include "GPU.h"
 
 #include "GPUAdapter.h"
@@ -100,3 +102,5 @@ RefPtr<GPUCompositorIntegration> GPU::createCompositorIntegration()
 }
 
 } // namespace WebCore
+
+#endif // ENABLE(WEBGPU)
